  "description": "3-phase panel power analyzer, Modbus RTU RS-485. FC04 read, FC10 write. Phase V/I/P/Q/PF/VA/cosφ + 3-phase totals (s32) at addr 0-124; scale per unit registers at 5500-5507. Total energy kWh/kvarh/kVAh at addr 1660-1777 (u32 integer part). Harmonics fundamentals at 4700-5067. Angle V/I at 6000-6010. Comms config at 10040.",
  "revision": 1,
  "source": "Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/circutor-cvm-b100-b150.toml; Source: circutor-cvm-b100-b150-instruction-manual.pdf (section 6.3, pp. 176-195). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation",
  "notes": [
    "Circutor CVM-B100/B150.",
    "Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.",
    "Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.",
    "Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.",
    "| Circutor CVM-B100 / CVM-B150 — Panel-Mount 3-Phase Power Analyzer (Modbus RTU RS-485)",
    "|",
    "| Source: circutor-cvm-b100-b150-instruction-manual.pdf (section 6.3, pp. 176-195)",
    "| Models: CVM-B100 (92mm panel), CVM-B150 (138mm panel)",
    "| Protocol: Modbus RTU or BACnet; FC04 read, FC10 write, 8N1 default (configurable)",
    "| Baud: 1200/2400/4800/9600/19200/38400/57600/76800/115200 (default 9600)",
    "| All MODBUS addresses are hexadecimal in source; converted to decimal here.",
    "| Each instantaneous value occupies 2 registers (s32). Real value = register_value × 10^unit_exponent,",
    "| where the unit exponent is stored per-channel at unit addresses (see \"Unit registers\" section).",
    "| Energy values occupy 3 registers: first 2 = integer part (u32), third = decimal part (u16).",
    "| Only integer part (u32) is listed here; decimal part is at address+2.",
    "| Harmonics: fundamental = 2-register s32; harmonics 2–50 = 1-register u16 each (consecutive).",
    "| Current energy has 3 tariff periods + Total; only Total is mapped here (Tariff 1 starts at addr 1300).",
    "| Unit register values at addr 5500–5507 give the power-of-10 exponent for each measurement type."
  ],
